From d5cbdf36b96490d035990ad9c58a5bfae57cb096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 12:10:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] t/steamvr_drv: Add $ORIGIN runtime path so bundled deps
 resolve in pressure-vessel

SteamVR's vrserver runs inside Valve's Steam Linux Runtime container,
which has neither the host's locally-built libraries nor its
LD_LIBRARY_PATH, so driver_monado.so fails to load whenever one of its
direct dependencies (libhidapi-libusb, libuvc, ...) is missing from the
runtime (issues #240, #423, #519). Adding $ORIGIN to the runtime path
lets a deployment bundle those dependencies next to the .so inside
steamvr-monado/bin/linux64/, which works from inside the sandbox without
depending on host paths or container configuration.

Since the plugin is installed via install(DIRECTORY) of the build
output, the build-tree binary ships verbatim and BUILD_RPATH is what
takes effect in installed copies; INSTALL_RPATH is set alongside it for
consistency should the install method ever change. Linux-only: $ORIGIN
is meaningless to dyld and Windows.

Note DT_RUNPATH is non-transitive: it covers driver_monado.so's direct
NEEDED entries, and a bundled library's own dependencies still resolve
against the runtime. That covers the reported failures, which are all
first-level.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
---
 src/xrt/targets/steamvr_drv/CMakeLists.txt | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/xrt/targets/steamvr_drv/CMakeLists.txt b/src/xrt/targets/steamvr_drv/CMakeLists.txt
index 52d6f5c77..6f5de0268 100644
--- a/src/xrt/targets/steamvr_drv/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/xrt/targets/steamvr_drv/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -65,6 +65,16 @@ set_target_properties(driver_monado PROPERTIES LIBRARY_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY "${PLUGI
 # don't add lib prefix to driver_monado.so
 set_target_properties(driver_monado PROPERTIES PREFIX "")
 
+# Add $ORIGIN to the runtime path so a deployment can bundle the driver's direct
+# dependencies (e.g. libhidapi-libusb) next to the .so, for use inside SteamVR's
+# Steam Linux Runtime (pressure-vessel) container, which lacks host-local libraries.
+# Note: the install(DIRECTORY) below ships the build-tree binary verbatim, so
+# BUILD_RPATH is what ends up in installed copies too; INSTALL_RPATH is set for
+# consistency should this ever switch to install(TARGETS).
+if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
+	set_target_properties(driver_monado PROPERTIES BUILD_RPATH "$ORIGIN" INSTALL_RPATH "$ORIGIN")
+endif()
+
 install(
 	DIRECTORY "${PROJECT_BINARY_DIR}/steamvr-monado"
 	DESTINATION "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/share"
-- 
